                                     # [joint-probe] orth-frac meter observes WITHOUT penalizing
                                     # (loss path skips at beta==0 -- beta=0 control stays a no-op)
 
+    # ═══ Physical-parameter learning rate (P1, implementation-plan/DECISIONS.md) ═══
+    # Separate optimizer group for log_params. None = one rate for everything
+    # (pre-P1 behaviour, bit-identical). The ANN needs ~1e-5 for K=0 routing
+    # stability (D-101/D-102) while theta needs large RELATIVE steps: at 1e-5 x
+    # 130 steps theta travels 0.13% of log space against a 10% detune, 75x short.
+    # 1e-3 is not a guess: train_param_recovery.py:143-155 recovers these same 14
+    # parameters, same log-reparameterization, from the same +-10% detune to 1e-7
+    # at LR=1e-3. No literature rule exists for this split (STATUS.md G7a: across
+    # six papers in the ancestry "parameter group" occurs zero times).
+    lr_theta: Optional[float] = None
+    # Adam eps for the log_params group ONLY (P1-e). Applied only when lr_theta is
+    # set, so runs without P1 are untouched. The PyTorch default 1e-8 is a FLOOR on
+    # the physical parameters, not a safeguard: measured |dL/dlog_params| runs
+    # 9.6e-13 to 2.6e-8, so the step lr*|g|/(|g|+eps) is attenuated by 9.6e-5 to
+    # 1.4e-2 on the stiffness/damping coordinates while the masses keep 0.47-0.72.
+    # At 1e-16 every coordinate steps at lr (measured, T1-p1-lr-theta.md L1c).
+    # NOTE this removes a stabiliser: if a coordinate's gradient reaches genuine
+    # zero the step becomes lr*sign(numerical noise). Approved by the user
+    # 2026-08-18 without the per-epoch |g| distribution first.
+    eps_theta: float = 1e-16
+
     # ═══ Fixed model dimensions ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
